ll_Connection","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A7227"}]}},"infoboxes":[{"name":"infobox titan","parameters":[{"name":"image","value_wikitext":"File:Bazela Insect.jpg","value_text":"File:Bazela Insect.jpg","links":[]},{"name":"attack","value_wikitext":"?","value_text":"?","links":[]},{"name":"defense","value_wikitext":"?","value_text":"?","links":[]},{"name":"type","value_wikitext":"[[Swara-Titan]]","value_text":"Swara-Titan","links":[{"target_title":"Swara-Titan","label":"Swara-Titan","target_id":"huntik:page:2842","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Swara-Titan","status":"resolved","href":"#/categories?name=Swara-Titans"}]},{"name":"size","value_wikitext":"","value_text":"","links":[]},{"name":"ability","value_wikitext":"Flight","value_text":"Flight","links":[]},{"name":"users","value_wikitext":"[[Harrison Fears]] <br> [[Tantras]] <br> [[The Betrayer]]","value_text":"Harrison Fears\nTantras\nThe Betrayer","links":[{"target_title":"Harrison Fears","label":"Harrison Fears","target_id":"huntik:page:4446","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Harrison_Fears","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4446"},{"target_title":"Tantras","label":"Tantras","target_id":"huntik:page:4559","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Tantras","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4559"},{"target_title":"The Betrayer","label":"The Betrayer","target_id":"huntik:page:4562","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Betrayer","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4562"}]},{"name":"height","value_wikitext":"","value_text":"","links":[]},{"name":"weight","value_wikitext":"","value_text":"","links":[]},{"name":"first","value_wikitext":"\"[[The Casterwill Connection]]\"","value_text":"\"The Casterwill Connection\"","links":[{"target_title":"The Casterwill Connection","label":"The Casterwill Connection","target_id":"huntik:page:7227","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Casterwill_Connection","status":"resolved","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A7227"}]}],"start":0,"end":292}],"sections":[{"heading":"History","level":2,"wikitext":"Bazela's Insects were ridden by [[Kiel]], [[Marduk]], and two [[Casterwill Hunters]]. Their destination was New York's cloisters to hunt out [[Focauld Casterwill]]. {{source|The Casterwill Connection}}\n\nA large number of Bazela's Insects were used by [[Tantras]] and the [[Silent Soldiers]] to attack the [[Casterwill family]] at the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. {{source|The Spiral War}}\n\nThey were later used by [[Harrison Fears]] and [[Rassimov]] to retrieve the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]]. After Rassimov was taken prisoner, Harrison sacrificed the energy of one of the Insects using [[Powermark]]. {{source|Rassimov's Secret}} \n\nAfter Harrison lost the Amulet of Bazela's Hive, the Betrayer took the Amulet, using the insect fliers to battle the [[Huntik Foundation]] and [[Casterwill family]]. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} {{Source|Dante's Return}}","text":"Bazela's Insects were ridden by Kiel, Marduk, and two Casterwill Hunters. Their destination was New York's cloisters to hunt out Focauld Casterwill. [The Casterwill Connection]\n\nA large number of Bazela's Insects were used by Tantras and the Silent Soldiers to attack the Casterwill family at the Fortress of Iron Will. [The Spiral War]\n\nThey were later used by Harrison Fears and Rassimov to retrieve the Necklace of Tutankhamun. After Rassimov was taken prisoner, Harrison sacrificed the energy of one of the Insects using Powermark. [Rassimov's Secret]\n\nAfter Harrison lost the Amulet of Bazela's Hive, the Betrayer took the Amulet, using the insect fliers to battle the Huntik Foundation and Casterwill family. [Lok and the Betrayer] [Dante's Return]"},{"heading":"Abilities","level":2,"wikitext":"The Insect Fliers sole purpose is that of a means of transport, for which it possesses great speed, able to travel across terrain in little time. They have the endurance to reach [[Cloisters|America]] {{source|The Casterwill Connection}} and [[Egypt]]. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}} They are also strong enough carry [[Seekers]], either by letting them ride on their backs or by carrying them in their arms. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Swara-Titans]]\n[[Category:Blood Spiral Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 2 Titans]]\n{{clear}}{{SwaraBox}}","text":"The Insect Fliers sole purpose is that of a means of transport, for which it possesses great speed, able to travel across terrain in little time. They have the endurance to reach America [The Casterwill Connection] and Egypt. [Rassimov's Secret] They are also strong enough carry Seekers, either by letting them ride on their backs or by carrying them in their arms. [Lok and the Betrayer]"}],"full_text":"Bazela's Insects are Swara-Titan fliers summoned by the Bazela's Hive Titan. Many Bazela's Insects may be deployed from a single mother Titan to transport Seekers across the globe or carry them into the heart of battle.\n\nHistory\n\nBazela's Insects were ridden by Kiel, Marduk, and two Casterwill Hunters. Their destination was New York's cloisters to hunt out Focauld Casterwill. [The Casterwill Connection]\n\nA large number of Bazela's Insects were used by Tantras and the Silent Soldiers to attack the Casterwill family at the Fortress of Iron Will. [The Spiral War]\n\nThey were later used by Harrison Fears and Rassimov to retrieve the Necklace of Tutankhamun. After Rassimov was taken prisoner, Harrison sacrificed the energy of one of the Insects using Powermark. [Rassimov's Secret]\n\nAfter Harrison lost the Amulet of Bazela's Hive, the Betrayer took the Amulet, using the insect fliers to battle the Huntik Foundation and Casterwill family. [Lok and the Betrayer] [Dante's Return]\n\nAbilities\n\nThe Insect Fliers sole purpose is that of a means of transport, for which it possesses great speed, able to travel across terrain in little time. They have the endurance to reach America [The Casterwill Connection] and Egypt. [Rassimov's Secret] They are also strong enough carry Seekers, either by letting them ride on their backs or by carrying them in their arms. [Lok and the Betrayer]","raw_wikitext":"{{infobox titan\n| image    = File:Bazela Insect.jpg\n| attack   = ?\n| defense  = ?\n| type     = [[Swara-Titan]] \n| size     = \n| ability  = Flight\n| users    = [[Harrison Fears]] <br> [[Tantras]] <br> [[The Betrayer]]\n| height   = \n| weight   = \n| first    = \"[[The Casterwill Connection]]\"\n}}'''Bazela's Insects''' are [[Swara-Titan]] fliers summoned by the [[Bazela's Hive]] [[Titan]]. Many Bazela's Insects may be deployed from a single mother Titan to transport [[Seekers]] across the globe or carry them into the heart of battle.\n\n== History ==\nBazela's Insects were ridden by [[Kiel]], [[Marduk]], and two [[Casterwill Hunters]]. Their destination was New York's cloisters to hunt out [[Focauld Casterwill]]. {{source|The Casterwill Connection}}\n\nA large number of Bazela's Insects were used by [[Tantras]] and the [[Silent Soldiers]] to attack the [[Casterwill family]] at the [[Fortress of Iron Will]]. {{source|The Spiral War}}\n\nThey were later used by [[Harrison Fears]] and [[Rassimov]] to retrieve the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]]. After Rassimov was taken prisoner, Harrison sacrificed the energy of one of the Insects using [[Powermark]]. {{source|Rassimov's Secret}} \n\nAfter Harrison lost the Amulet of Bazela's Hive, the Betrayer took the Amulet, using the insect fliers to battle the [[Huntik Foundation]] and [[Casterwill family]]. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} {{Source|Dante's Return}}\n\n== Abilities ==\nThe Insect Fliers sole purpose is that of a means of transport, for which it possesses great speed, able to travel across terrain in little time. They have the endurance to reach [[Cloisters|America]] {{source|The Casterwill Connection}} and [[Egypt]]. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}} They are also strong enough carry [[Seekers]], either by letting them ride on their backs or by carrying them in their arms. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}\n[[Category:Titans]]\n[[Category:Swara-Titans]]\n[[Category:Blood Spiral Titans]]\n[[Category:Season 2 Titans]]\n{{clear}}{{SwaraBox}}","categories":["Blood Spiral Titans","Season 2 Titans","Swara-Titans","Titans"],"links":[{"target_id":"huntik:page:2842","status":"resolved","target_title":"Swara-Titan","label":"Swara-Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Swara-Titan","href":"#/categories?name=Swara-Titans"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:4446","status":"resolved","target_title":"Harrison Fears","label":"Harrison Fears","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Harrison_Fears","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4446"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:4559","status":"resolved","target_title":"Tantras","label":"Tantras","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Tantras","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4559"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:4562","status":"resolved","target_title":"The Betrayer","label":"The Betrayer","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Betrayer","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4562"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:7227","status":"resolved","target_title":"The Casterwill Connection","label":"The Casterwill Connection","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/The_Casterwill_Connection","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A7227"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2842","status":"resolved","target_title":"Swara-Titan","label":"Swara-Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Swara-Titan","href":"#/categories?name=Swara-Titans"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:4611","status":"resolved","target_title":"Bazela's Hive","label":"Bazela's Hive","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Bazela%27s_Hive","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A4611"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:2010","status":"resolved","target_title":"Titan","label":"Titan","target_url":"https://huntik.fandom.com/wiki/Titan","href":"#/entry/huntik%3Apage%3A2010"},{"target_id":"huntik:page:1997",